    "best": "Walk the old town, since the main sights are compact. Use buses or taxis for longer trips.",
    "modes": [
      {
        "mode": "Metro",
        "has": true,
        "text": "One line runs south-west to south-east and misses the old town. Tickets cost €1.30 for one zone."
      },
      {
        "mode": "Bus",
        "has": true,
        "text": "City buses are frequent and cover most of the city. A single fare is €1.40, or €0.35–0.38 with a rechargeable bonobus card."
      },
      {
        "mode": "Taxi / ride apps",
        "has": true,
        "best": true,
        "text": "Taxis are easy to find. Cabify, Uber, Bolt and FreeNow all operate, and Cabify is the local favourite. Check the fare before you ride."
      },
      {
        "mode": "Rental car",
        "has": true,
        "text": "Driving in the old city is tricky. Park in a hotel garage, and never leave anything in the car because break-ins are common."
      },
      {
        "mode": "Walking",
        "has": true,
        "best": true,
        "text": "Walking is the best way to see the sights, since the main points are compact."
      },
      {
        "mode": "Tram",
        "has": true,
        "text": "Trams run about 2 km from Prado de San Sebastián to Plaza Nueva, past the cathedral. Most visitors walk this stretch instead."
      },
